00:00:05.829 --> 00:00:07.990 align:start position:0%
european ministers responsible for  energy policy meet in luxembourg on  friday june 7 to sign off on an approach  for completing the eu's internal energy  market by 2014.  the aim is to ensure that no member  state is left off europe's gas and  electricity grids after 2015 and to  improve the rights of consumers  global warming and recent energy supply  disputes have raised the awareness in  europe of a need to have sustainable  secure and competitive energy sources  the internal energy market plan whose  implementation will be reviewed at the  end of next year will help the eu shift  to a low carbon economy and make it less  reliant on unstable energy providers  abroad  the ministers will place emphasis on  energy savings through smart appliances  and the need to educate consumers so  they can make informed choices  they will also underline people's rights  to affordable energy stressing the need  for transparency equality and  predictability when it comes to  electricity or gas contracts billing and  price schemes
 

